tive-execution interface facts, not whole-task completion. Exact source predicates and frozen evidence: specs/requirement-reconciliation/profile-system/gap-completion.edn, mapping ai/replay-evaluation-artifacts; all attached contextual and negative predicates remain required. No implementation acceptance is inferred.\n\nCriterion `domain/support-agent-integration`: Execute and evaluate declared support triage with prompt provenance, structured-output/taint, durable graph/replay, tool policy and required refund/review transitions. Accepted fixture: Run support triage with prompt provenance, structured validated outputs, retrieval trust, durable replay, tool policy and explicit refund human-review transition. Negative fixture: Reject prompt policy escalation, unvalidated output, missing tool grant or write tool without required review. Required evidence: agent/tool/prompt/memory/review graph, eval and replay reports; bind source/compiler/profile/target/provider identities, source-mapped stable diagnostics and every applicable source facet field/exception/negative condition listed for this criterion in specs/requirement-reconciliation/domain-gap-completion.edn. Dependencies consume schema, workflow outputs under their stated contracts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Status: Open; implementation acceptance unassessed.",
