   "Actual service link/load inspection for every claimed profile/target and forbidden-service rejection. R1/R2/R4: explicit family selection and compatible composition; linked/generated/delegated/external/forbidden service records consumed by backend, package, observability, conformance and self-hosting tools; runtime-none entry/reset/interrupt/ABI, sections, memory map, alignment and required target stack evidence; generated checks and panic helpers with provenance. Reject hidden GC, allocator, scheduler, reflection, eval, host IO and hosted-profile leakage; unsupported dynamic forms reject unless eliminated with evidence. Dependencies: Lower supplies target ABI/artifacts, Legality supplies profile facts, and Build supplies package policy; no product ISA or platform choice is made here. Residual criterion runtime/family-composition: For each claimed profile/target pair, resolve the selected combination of R1 runtime families under profile compatibility and package policy, emitting the family-selection record and linked/generated/delegated/external/forbidden service table. Exercise an allowed combination and reject incompatible combinations, undeclared providers and hidden universal-runtime dependencies. Every selected service and typed host adapter retains its effects, capability hook or applicable static proof, startup/failure model and provenance; listing families without checking the combination is not acceptance. Residual criterion runtime/manifest-consumption: Have backend, package, observability, conformance and self-hosting consumers read the emitted runtime manifest and cross-check it against the actual selected service/helper/provider graph. Emit consumer agreement evidence for family/profile/target, service classification, linked support objects, generated helpers, delegated typed adapters, external providers, forbidden services, capability enforcement hooks or static proofs, startup/initialization/cleanup/failure policy and runtime diagnostic schema/provenance. Reject an absent/unreadable manifest, omitted or contradictory service/provider, hidden forbidden dependency, missing enforcement hook/proof or lost artifact/source-origin edge. A manifest link or producer-only record cannot establish consumer integration. Native backend integration includes C and LLVM artifacts for the claimed target matrix; fixture inspection alone does not claim those targets implemented. Foundation requirement gravity/explicit-runtime-service-dependencies: For every actually used runtime service, emit the selected runtime/provider, service contract/version, effect/grant, profile and source dependency and demonstrate its use across that declared boundary. Refusals: Reject an undeclared allocator, IO, reflection, dynamic dispatch or hosted service, including a transitive service in a no-runtime artifact, before claiming support. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks - Expanded source profile/effect/grant facts and checked/delegated/rejected legality products; lower/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/lower1-validate-lowering-inputs - Verified MIR/domain-operation disposition matrix and target/provider/preservation inputs. Foundation requirement gravity/runtime-manifest-closure: Close the selected runtime manifest transitively over actual linked/loaded services and providers, declared effects/grants, profiles and source dependencies; compare manifest declarations with the produced artifact's service usage. Refusals: Reject an undeclared transitive allocator/IO/reflection/dispatch/thread dependency or an unavailable service in a no-runtime profile; a chosen runtime label cannot authorize the missing service. Evidence: retain the exact source/compiler/profile/target and applicable provider/checker identities, actual positive products and negative diagnostics for this criterion. Consume these actual dependency artifacts (not whole-component completion): lower/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/lower1-validate-lowering-inputs - Verified MIR/domain-operation disposition matrix and target/provider/preservation inputs; legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks - Expanded source profile/effect/grant facts and checked/delegated/rejected legality products; build/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/close-reproducibility-and-target-matrix - Locked source/compiler/provider/target build graph and canonical rebuild comparison. Criterion `runtime/freestanding-layout`: Provide target-accurate memory/section/entry/interrupt/ABI records and required stack-bound evidence for freestanding execution. Accepted fixture: Emit target-accurate memory/section/entry/interrupt/ABI and applicable stack evidence for declared no-runtime/firmware/kernel execution. Negative fixture: Reject inconsistent target layout/ABI, missing entry/vector/section records and hidden hosted-service dependencies. Required evidence: freestanding layout/startup manifest and target-bound acceptance/rejection fixtures; bind source/compiler/profile/target/provider identities, source-mapped stable diagnostics and every applicable source facet field/exception/negative condition listed for this criterion in specs/requirement-reconciliation/domain-gap-completion.edn. Dependencies consume lower/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/lower2-derive-abi-and-layout, legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks outputs under their stated contracts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Status: Open; implementation acceptance unassessed.",
